                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "45446007",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198156688841",
                            "num_reviews": 147,
                            "playtime_forever": 749,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 740,
                            "last_played": 1576613237
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I would love to enjoy this game, but even for early access it is over-simplified, lacks atmosphere and in general is no fun at all.:\n1. you start from the scratch, but in fact you don't build any train station, just terminus, which is unusual kind of train station\n2. you can't freely plan the tracks, thus you are forced to build an open-space kind of station\n3. you can't create any buildings (just put up walls, which have no real use)\n4. a lot of elements are ready-made object that can't be modified (f.e. you can put ticket booth, but can't build indoor ticket counter, you can't just assign room to be converted into bar or toilet, you can only place them as an object)\n5. you can adapt link between arriving trains and buses, but you can't see the time table for both of them at the same time\n6. you have to build separate bus stops for each kind of buses, which makes no sense at all\n7. changes of the timetable are more annoying than add anything to the gameplay\n\nAnd worst of all is that the game has no purpose - you build elements, collect money, build some more and... that's it! It doesn't feel that you have influence on most of the game mechanics",
                        "timestamp_created": 1540550570,
